    {
      "id": "claim_0fbffafac8db4fe8a17333796745cff8",
      "statement": "The `start_sync` command is a thin Tauri adapter to `Synchronization::start`; the service requires a watched folder, scans and admits its work, and atomically claims a running lifecycle before pipeline execution. A concurrent producer joins the claimed lifecycle rather than receiving an independent run, while a failed manual run clears the guard, persists/emits a failed snapshot when possible, audits the abort, and returns the error.",
